wisp (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Manifest format 1: 'format = 1' on the first line, unknown keys are errors.
  * wisp build refuses a btrfs subvolume root, an invalid key provider and
    archive entries that do not fit the newc format; recognises the root
    logical volume without a device-mapper UUID.
  * wisp-init: the provider's key is read into one fixed buffer.
  * Documentation brought in line with the code.

 -- Richard Robert Reitz <reitzrobert77@gmail.com>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 23:30:00 +0200

wisp (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release: reproducible initramfs builder and pure-Go /init.
    Coldplug without udev, LUKS2 without cryptsetup, linear LVM without
    lvm2, key sources none/passphrase/credential and external key providers.

 -- Richard Robert Reitz <reitzrobert77@gmail.com>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 13:21:50 +0200
